Z||000000||Julian||08-20-2001||07:48 PM||||Looking to put a Grand Am CD stereo in my 88 Fiero (or any red GM light CD radio)....where do I get the harness adaptor?  Are there different adapters for different year radios? Do I also need antenna adaptor? And the big question is how do I hook my factory sub & amp to it? Feel free to e-mail any complicated techno stuff to julian60@hotmail.com (rather than take up too much space in here)... thanks for the time everyone. (almost forgot) how can I clear a theft lock if I buy one "as is"?<P>Julian<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/meralogo.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000001||PBJ||08-20-2001||08:34 PM||||I can help you with this.  You can get the adaptors at wallmart, and you will need an antenna adapter as well, with your factory sub you will need to change the orange wires from sub (hot at all times) to pink (hot in run) unless you don't mind boosting your car in the morning (past experience). You can get a red lite radio out of any Pontiac and if the theft light is on I can walk you through it too.  I have a 98 sunfire cass in mine and a 96 G/prix cd in my wifes with factory sub.<P>do a search on the subject tooooo. in technical area.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/petesigsm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
